   pattern         total  per-win   alpha (rel.disp)     latent_ac(lag1)   phi
   pat_nea_all     33805     8.45    0.259 +/- 0.012   +0.204 +/- 0.028    3.17
   pat_den_only    61517    15.38    0.096 +/- 0.007   +0.292 +/- 0.028    2.46
   pat_all_arch    41146    10.29    0.393 +/- 0.015   +0.180 +/- 0.022    4.97
   pat_alt_only    18191     4.55    0.275 +/- 0.016   +0.368 +/- 0.034    2.23
   pat_vin_only    15127     3.78    0.259 +/- 0.025   +0.380 +/- 0.036    1.94
   pat_chag_only   13076     3.27    0.316 +/- 0.023   +0.436 +/- 0.036    2.01

   CONTRASTS on alpha (jackknifed as a single statistic):
     alpha(pat_nea_all) - alpha(pat_alt_only ) = -0.017 +/- 0.021   z = -0.78
     alpha(pat_nea_all) - alpha(pat_all_arch ) = -0.134 +/- 0.017   z = -7.74
     alpha(pat_nea_all) - alpha(pat_den_only ) = +0.162 +/- 0.013   z = +12.26
   vs pat_alt_only : drift/error control -> Model A predicts > 0
   vs pat_all_arch : same depth/genome count on the SHARED archaic branch;
                     note Model A also feeds this pattern, so it is a
                     conservative (signal-contaminated) control
   vs pat_den_only : Model B's own signature -> Model A predicts ~0,
                     Model B predicts < 0

-- T2  tail symmetry at the pooled q=0.99 threshold ----------------------
   R_den   tail mass 0.0107 +/- 0.0018
   R_alt   tail mass 0.0085 +/- 0.0014
   R_vin   tail mass 0.0105 +/- 0.0016
   R_chag  tail mass 0.0103 +/- 0.0017
   Denisovan - Neanderthal-mean = +0.0010 +/- 0.0016  (z = +0.63)
   z >> 0 favours Model B; z ~ 0 is equally consistent with Model A and the null.

-- T3  cross-lineage covariance ------------------------------------------
   corr(R_den, R_nea) = +0.8303 +/- 0.0090
   Compare against the simulated M0/M1/M2/M3 values (sims/superarchaic_sim.py).

